.TH MOM 8 "2026-09-22" "mom 0.2.23" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
mom \- Meta Overlay Manager: install packages without root access
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mom
.RB [ \-y ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-recommends ]
.B install
.IR package " [" package "...]"
.br
.B mom
.RB [ \-y ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-recommends ]
.B update
.IR package " [" package "...]"
.br
.B mom
.RB [ \-y ]
.B upgrade
.br
.B mom
.B refresh
.br
.B mom
.B \-\-check
.br
.B mom
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mom
(Meta Overlay Manager) allows non-root users to install and update packages
on systems where they lack root access. It delegates to
.BR apt-get (8)
on Debian/Ubuntu systems and
.BR dnf (8)
on RHEL/Rocky Linux systems.
.PP
.B mom
must be deployed as a setuid-root binary. Only members of the configured
group (default:
.BR mom )
may run it. Every subcommand, including
.B refresh
and
.BR \-\-check ,
requires membership in that group.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI "install " "package " "[package...]"
Install one or more packages. Package names are validated and checked
against the deny list before any package manager is invoked.
.TP
.BI "update " "package " "[package...]"
Refresh the package repository metadata, then update the named packages.
Each package must already be installed; mom will error out rather than
silently install an unlisted package.
.TP
.B upgrade
Refresh the package repository metadata, then upgrade all installed
packages (\fBapt-get upgrade\fR or \fBdnf upgrade\fR).
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh package repository metadata only (\fBapt-get update\fR or
\fBdnf makecache\fR).
.PP
On Debian/Ubuntu, \fBinstall\fR, \fBupdate\fR and \fBupgrade\fR first check
for packages left in an intermediate state by an interrupted dpkg run (for
example a \fBmom install\fR stopped with Ctrl+C, or a debconf prompt nobody
could answer). Half-installed packages are unpacked again with
\fBapt-get install \-\-reinstall\fR; these and any packages merely awaiting
configuration are then finished with \fBdpkg \-\-configure \-a\fR. This is
logged as a separate \fIrepair\fR operation.
.PP
Repair never reinstalls a package whose interrupted operation was a removal
or purge, and it applies the deny list to every broken package name before
touching it. Either case refuses the caller's entire operation with a message
to contact the system administrator, rather than silently completing or
reversing work outside what the caller asked for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Suppress interactive prompts. Passed directly to
.B apt-get
or
.BR dnf .
Also selects non-interactive mode for the package manager itself (see
.B NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
below), even when run from a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recommends
Skip recommended and optional dependencies. Passed as
.B \-\-no\-install\-recommends
to
.B apt-get
and as
.B \-\-setopt=install_weak_deps=False
to
.BR dnf .
Useful for minimal installs where disk space or attack surface matters.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the configuration file, deny list and binary permissions without
performing any package operations. Prints a summary of all checks performed.
Intended for sysadmin use; requires group membership like every other
operation.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
mom never lets the caller adjudicate a
.BR dpkg (1)
conffile prompt. On every
.B apt-get
install, update, upgrade or repair reinstall, and on every
.B "dpkg \-\-configure \-a"
mom runs, it passes
.BR \-\-force\-confdef ,
.B \-\-force\-confold
and
.B \-\-no\-pager
(as
.B "\-o Dpkg::Options::="
options for
.BR apt-get )
unconditionally, in
.B every
mode, interactive or not. dpkg's conffile prompt offers
.B Z
(spawn a root shell) and
.B D
(view a diff through a pager, and
.BR less (1)
allows
.B !cmd
shell escapes) \(em a mom caller is not the system administrator and must
never be offered either, so existing configuration files (or the package
default, if unmodified) are always kept automatically. Because mom cannot
tell a conffile change the admin wants from one they would reject, it always
keeps what is on disk: the new upstream version is left alongside as
.I *.dpkg-dist
(or
.I *.ucf-dist
, see below) for the admin to review and merge by hand \(em it never takes
effect on its own. (
.B \-\-no\-pager
requires
.BR dpkg " " >=\~1.19.2 ,
which every distribution mom currently packages for already ships; do not
add an older Debian/Ubuntu release as a packaging target without first
confirming its dpkg supports the option, or dpkg will refuse to run at all.)
.PP
On
.BR apt-get ,
mom additionally sets
.B UCF_FORCE_CONFFOLD=1
, because
.BR ucf (1)
(used by many package postinst scripts to manage files under
.IR /etc )
has its own conffile prompt with a "start a new shell" choice that also runs
a root shell on the caller's terminal; this keeps the existing file instead,
matching
.BR \-\-force\-confold .
It also sets
.B NEEDRESTART_MODE=l
so
.BR needrestart (1)
only lists services that need restarting and never prompts for, or performs,
a restart on the caller's behalf \(em this overrides an admin's own
.B needrestart
policy for mom-initiated runs specifically: even if the system is configured
to restart affected services automatically, a service using stale, just-updated
libraries keeps running its old code until the admin (or a reboot) restarts
it.
.PP
Separately, mom always sets
.B DEBIAN_FRONTEND
on
.BR apt-get :
.B noninteractive
whenever
.B \-y
is given, or when standard input is not a terminal (scripts, CI, AI agent
sandboxes), so a debconf prompt nobody can answer never hangs the caller; and
otherwise (an interactive terminal, no
.BR \-y )
.B dialog
\(em left unset, debconf would use whatever frontend is configured in its own
database, which may be
.B Editor
(runs
.BR /usr/bin/editor ,
e.g.\&
.BR vim (1)
running
.B :!sh
, as root), Web, Gnome or Kde; none of those are safe to hand an unprivileged
caller.
.B dialog
itself falls back to Readline and then Teletype when no dialog program or
terminal is usable, and neither of those can shell out. In this interactive
case the caller's
.B TERM
value is also validated and passed through to the child so prompts render
correctly, and the caller may then answer any ordinary (non-conffile)
debconf question the package being installed or upgraded asks \(em for
example whether to install a setuid helper, or which device to write a
bootloader to. This does not allow a shell-out or bypass the deny list, but
it is package-configuration policy chosen by an authorized user rather than
the sysadmin; deny specific packages, or use
.B \-y
or a non-TTY caller, to avoid it.
.PP
In every mode, mom also fixes
.BR PAGER ,
.B SYSTEMD_PAGER
and
.B MANPAGER
to
.BR cat ,
and sets
.BR LESSSECURE=1 ,
so that any helper program which still tries to page output cannot hand the
caller a shell escape as root. For
.B apt-get
specifically, mom also sets
.BR APT_LISTCHANGES_FRONTEND=none ,
.B APT_LISTBUGS_FRONTEND=none
and
.B DPKG_PAGER=cat
, since apt-listchanges' default frontend runs a pager as root against the
caller's terminal and apt-listbugs can launch a browser. No other caller
environment variable is passed in any mode.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B mom
reads
.I /etc/mom/mom.conf
at startup. If the file does not exist, safe defaults are used.
The file must be owned by root and must not be group- or world-writable.
Format: one
.BI key " = " value
pair per line. Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.
.PP
Supported keys:
.TP
.B group
Name of the Unix group whose members may run
.BR mom .
Default:
.BR mom .
.TP
.B deny_list
Path to the package deny list file. May reside on a shared filesystem.
Default:
.IR /etc/mom/deny.list .
.TP
.B log_file
Path to the JSON audit log.
Default:
.IR /var/log/mom.log .
.TP
.B http_proxy
HTTP proxy URL passed to
.B apt-get
/
.BR dnf .
Not set by default.
.TP
.B https_proxy
HTTPS proxy URL passed to
.B apt-get
/
.BR dnf .
Not set by default.
.SH DENY LIST
The deny list file (default
.IR /etc/mom/deny.list )
contains one or more entries per line, separated by spaces. Entries are glob patterns matched against
package names. Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments. Empty lines are ignored.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Block network scanners
nmap
wireshark

# Block all Python development headers
python3-*

# Block all -dev packages
*-dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
The deny list file must be owned by root, with group root or the configured
.B mom
group. It must not be group- or world-writable. If the file does not exist,
all packages are permitted (subject to other access controls).
.SH INSTALLATION & SETUP
.SS "1. Create the mom group"
.nf
groupadd mom
.fi
.SS "2. Install the binary"
.nf
install -o root -g mom -m 4750 /path/to/mom /usr/bin/mom
.fi
.PP
Mode 4755 (owner root:root) also works, but gains nothing: mom still
requires membership in the configured group for every subcommand.
.SS "3. Create the configuration directory"
.nf
mkdir -p /etc/mom
chown root:root /etc/mom
chmod 755 /etc/mom
.fi
.SS "4. Create the deny list"
.nf
touch /etc/mom/deny.list
chown root:mom /etc/mom/deny.list
chmod 640 /etc/mom/deny.list
.fi
.SS "5. Create the log file"
.nf
touch /var/log/mom.log
chown root:root /var/log/mom.log
chmod 640 /var/log/mom.log
.fi
.SS "6. Add users to the mom group"
.nf
usermod -aG mom alice
usermod -aG mom bob
.fi
.SH SECURITY
.B mom
is a setuid-root binary. The following security measures are applied at runtime:
.IP \(bu 2
The caller's entire environment is discarded before invoking
.B apt-get
or
.BR dnf .
The child receives only fixed constants \(em pager/helper-frontend safety
variables in every mode, plus, on apt, a fixed
.B DEBIAN_FRONTEND
(always
.B noninteractive
or
.B dialog ,
never unset and never caller-derived) \(em and, only on an interactive run, a
validated caller
.B TERM
(see
.B NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
above). No other caller environment variable ever reaches the child.
.IP \(bu 2
dpkg conffile prompts are never shown to the caller:
.BR \-\-force\-confdef ,
.B \-\-force\-confold
and
.B \-\-no\-pager
are passed on every
.B apt-get
and
.B dpkg
invocation, in every mode, so a caller can never reach dpkg's root-shell
(\fBZ\fR) or pager-escape (\fBD\fR) conffile prompt options.
.IP \(bu 2
Package manager binaries are called via hardcoded absolute paths.
.IP \(bu 2
Arguments are passed as discrete
.BR execve (2)
argv entries — never via a shell.
.IP \(bu 2
All supplemental groups are dropped immediately at startup.
.IP \(bu 2
Package names are validated against a strict regular expression before use.
.IP \(bu 2
All operations (including denied attempts) are logged to
.I /var/log/mom.log
and syslog.
.PP
See
.I /usr/share/doc/mom/SECURITY.md
for the full threat model and security analysis.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/mom
The setuid-root binary.
.TP
.I /etc/mom/mom.conf
Configuration file. Must be owned by root.
.TP
.I /etc/mom/deny.list
Package deny list. Must be owned by root (group root or mom).
.TP
.I /var/log/mom.log
JSON audit log.
.TP
.I /etc/logrotate.d/mom
Log rotation configuration.
